# Data Models Reference

Source of truth: `app/models.py`. Read it directly when in doubt — never trust docs over the actual model.

## Model Hierarchy

```
Subject (id: string, e.g. 'MATC')
  └── Topic (subject_id, sort_order)
        └── Subtopic (topic_id, hidden, sort_order)

Chapter (subject_id, sort_order)
  └── Subchapter (chapter_id, hidden, sort_order)

Question (qid, subject, source, year, paper, section, qno, q_type, level, ...)
  ├── major_topic_id → Topic
  ├── major_subtopic_id → Subtopic  (must belong to major_topic)
  ├── minor_topics → [Topic]  (M2M via question_minor_topics)
  ├── subtopics → [Subtopic]  (M2M via question_subtopics)
  ├── chapter_id → Chapter
  ├── subchapter_id → Subchapter
  └── assets → [QuestionAsset]

QuestionAsset (question_id, asset_type, file_format, language, file_path, part_number)

User (username, password_hash, is_super_admin)
  └── subject_permissions → [UserSubjectPermission]

UserSubjectPermission (user_id, subject_id, role)  — role: 'viewer'|'user'|'admin'
SavedFilter (user_id, name, filter_data JSON)
GeneratedFile (user_id, display_name, filename, status, filter_data, generation_options JSON, ...)
```

## Key Question Fields
| Field | Notes |
|---|---|
| `qid` | Unique string ID, indexed. Format: `MATC_DSE_2024_P1_Q5` |
| `source` | `DSE`, `CE`, `AL`, `QB` |
| `q_type` | `MC`, `CQ`, or NULL (auto-set by ingestor for MATC only) |
| `level` | 1–3 or NULL (manually tagged) |
| `section` | Free text (e.g. `A`, `Section I`) |
| `correct_percentage` | 0–100 or NULL (public exam correct rate) |
| `answer` | Text answer (alternative to ANS image) |
| `comment` | Notes/commentary text |

## QuestionAsset Constraints
- `asset_type`: `QUE`, `ANS`, `SOL`
- `file_format`: `IMG`, `DOC`
- `language`: `EN`, `CH`, `BI`
- `part_number`: int starting at 1 (for multi-image questions)
- Unique constraint: `(question_id, asset_type, language, file_format, part_number)`
- `file_path` stored as forward-slash relative path from `SOURCE_PATH`

## Permission Checks (User model methods)
- `user.has_subject_access(subject_id)` — any access (viewer/user/admin)
- `user.is_subject_admin(subject_id)` — admin role or super admin
- `user.can_generate()` — has 'user' or 'admin' role for ANY subject
- `user.is_all_view_only()` — all permissions are 'viewer'
- `user.get_subject_roles()` → `{subject_id: role}`

## GeneratedFile Status Flow
`pending` → `generating` → `completed` | `failed`

Stale `pending`/`generating` records are reset to `failed` on app startup (in `create_app()`).
